{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-8","id":"msg_014FgQ6eAKgrUQ1suHNbaKAk","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The fix is complete and consistent with the file's existing `fs` usage. Here's my analysis.\n\n## Root cause\n\nDuckLake writes each table's data files into a **directory** (`<data_path>/main/<table>/`), not a single file. The COPY operator is configured in rotation mode and points at that directory:\n\n- `src/storage/ducklake_insert.cpp:563-573` — for unpartitioned inserts DuckLake sets `rotate = true`, `file_size_bytes = target_file_size`, and `file_path = copy_input.data_path` (the table directory, trailing separator stripped). It also sets `overwrite_mode = COPY_OVERWRITE_OR_IGNORE` (line 574).\n\nBecause `Rotate()` is true, DuckDB treats `file_path` as an output directory in `PhysicalCopyToFile::GetGlobalSinkState` (`src/execution/operator/persistent/physical_copy_to_file.cpp:2589-2611`):\n\n```cpp\nif (!fs.IsRemoteFile(file_path)) {\n    if (fs.FileExists(file_path)) {                 // <-- the trap\n        if (overwrite_mode == COPY_OVERWRITE) { fs.RemoveFile(file_path); }\n        else { throw IOException(\"...it exists and is a file, not a directory!...\"); }\n    }\n}\nif (!fs.DirectoryExists(file_path)) { fs.CreateDirectory(file_path); }\nelse { CheckDirectory(...); }\n```\n\nThe flow on each INSERT:\n1. **First INSERT:** `FileExists(\"<data_path>/main/events\")` → false (nothing exists), `DirectoryExists` → false, so `CreateDirectory` makes the directory and parquet files are written into it. Succeeds.\n2. **Second INSERT:** `FileExists(\"<data_path>/main/events\")` returns **true** — even though it's now a directory. Since `overwrite_mode` is `COPY_OVERWRITE_OR_IGNORE` (≠ `COPY_OVERWRITE`), it throws the exact reported error.\n\nWhy `FileExists` lies on a directory: the call chain is `WebFileSystem::FileExists` (`lib/src/io/web_filesystem.cc:1002-1006`) → `duckdb_web_fs_file_exists` (`lib/js-stubs.js:66-69`) → `DUCKDB_RUNTIME.checkFile`. The node runtime's `checkFile` (`packages/duckdb-wasm/src/bindings/runtime_node.ts:296-305`) implemented this as:\n\n```ts\nreturn fs.existsSync(path);\n```\n\n`fs.existsSync` returns `true` for **any** existing path — files *and* directories. So once the table directory exists, `FileExists` wrongly reports it as a file. (The symmetric bug exists in `checkDirectory` at lines 233-242, which would report a regular file as a directory.)\n\nThis is a node-runtime-only manifestation: the in-memory `MemoryFileSystem::DirectoryExists` always returns `true` and `FileExists` checks an explicit file map, so the directory/file confusion doesn't arise there.\n\n## Fix\n\nIn `packages/duckdb-wasm/src/bindings/runtime_node.ts`, `checkFile` now stats the path and returns true only for a regular file; `checkDirectory` likewise returns true only for a directory:\n\n```ts\ncheckFile: (...) => {\n    const path = decodeText(...);\n    const stats = fs.statSync(path, { throwIfNoEntry: false });\n    return stats !== undefined && stats.isFile();\n}\ncheckDirectory: (...) => {\n    const path = decodeText(...);\n    const stats = fs.statSync(path, { throwIfNoEntry: false });\n    return stats !== undefined && stats.isDirectory();\n}\n```\n\n`{ throwIfNoEntry: false }` makes `statSync` return `undefined` instead of throwing for missing paths (preserving the old \"returns false when absent\" behavior), and is supported by the workspace's `@types/node` v22. This matches the existing `fs`/`fs.fstatSync` usage in the same file. After the fix, the second INSERT's `FileExists` correctly returns `false`, control falls through to the `DirectoryExists` → `CheckDirectory` branch, and the write proceeds.\n\nNote: I could not run a full typecheck/build — the workspace has no installed `node_modules` — but the change uses only standard `fs.Stats` APIs already present elsewhere in the file.\n\n## Sources\n- github.com/duckdb/ducklake · src/storage/ducklake_insert.cpp · 557-574 (rotate/file_path/overwrite_mode setup)\n- github.com/duckdb/duckdb · src/execution/operator/persistent/physical_copy_to_file.cpp · 2589-2611 (`GetGlobalSinkState` FileExists/DirectoryExists/throw)\n- github.com/duckdb/duckdb-wasm · lib/src/io/web_filesystem.cc · 1002-1006 (`WebFileSystem::FileExists`), 962-968 (`DirectoryExists`/`CreateDirectory`)\n- github.com/duckdb/duckdb-wasm · lib/js-stubs.js · 47-49, 66-69 (`duckdb_web_fs_file_exists`/`_directory_create` → runtime)\n- github.com/duckdb/duckdb-wasm · packages/duckdb-wasm/src/bindings/runtime_node.ts · 233-242 (`checkDirectory`), 296-305 (`checkFile`), 1 (`import fs`) — edited\n- github.com/duckdb/duckdb-wasm · lib/src/io/memory_filesystem.cc · 128-131, 165-167 (memory FS behaves differently → node-only bug)\n- github.com/duckdb/duckdb-wasm · packages/duckdb-wasm-app/package.json · 45 (`@types/node` ^22 supports `throwIfNoEntry`)"}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":682,"cache_read_input_tokens":63653,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":682},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"f33719cd-2282-4f92-8bfc-f8afcbe3306b","uuid":"c6350971-6ca8-4d83-912f-1fd2de55b3be","request_id":"req_011CbqyuTUr78mbxwWsUUjzD"}
